  "kind": "pose",
  "note": "For any quadruped. Folds down the way a deer, dog or cat lies: forelegs first, each folded at elbow and carpus with the hoof or paw tucked back under the chest, then the hind end, the hind feet stepping forward; chest and belly on the ground, hind legs folded out to one side each. Holds, then rises hind end first. The hold is a flat pair of keys so a game can cut it into down / rest / up. `under` sets each forefoot against its shoulder whatever stance the mesh was modelled in, and `ground` brings a hind foot joint that is really an ankle (a hare's) down to the floor.",
